# Fetched data is REPRODUCIBLE — re-downloadable from the authority — so the big ones stay
# out of git. Everything under source/ is a fetch away; everything under ../curated/ is not
# and is tracked deliberately.
#
# These patterns used to be bare names (`temp_bc_data/`, `*.gpkg`) and did not survive the
# move into source/: hydat.sqlite3 (1.2 GB) and 2,600 bathymetry PDFs were staged in one
# `git add`. Anchored and explicit now.
source/temp_bc_data/
source/bathymetry_pdfs/
source/hydat.sqlite3
# a kept previous HYDAT (update-hydat.sh / T301 keep the old archive as hydat.<YYYYMMDD>.sqlite3, 1.2 GB)
source/hydat.*.sqlite3
source/*.gpkg
source/*.pmtiles

# Run timing (PSF, 2026-10-24 owner): the Explorer pages are NOT tracked — the repo is public and PSF's permission
# covers the data we parse, not re-hosting their pages. Only fetched.json (what was fetched, when) is tracked; the
# pages and the 748-tile cache stay local and are re-fetched by pipeline.runtiming.fetch.
source/runtiming/*.html
source/runtiming/cu_tiles/
# DFO NuSEDS (Open Government Licence – Canada, T162): 227 MB of CSV, re-fetched by pipeline.runtiming.fetch.nuseds;
# only the parsed timings (source/runtiming/timing.json, T331) are tracked.
source/runtiming/dfo/
# Steelhead evidence (pipeline/regs/steelhead/known_waters.py): the accessibility model (6.6 GB)
# and ~17,000 DataBC records, both re-fetched by the script when missing.
source/steelhead/
# The pinned Protomaps glyphs + sprites (P18, pipeline/deliver/tiles/assets.py): a fetch away, 13 MB.
source/map-assets/
*.gpkg
*.pmtiles

# Generated: candidates awaiting promotion, cleaned municipal layers. Regenerable by
# definition — the promoted answers live in ../curated/.
# `generated/*`, not `generated/` — git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# `!generated/README.md` under a bare `generated/` rule is silently dead. Excluding the
# CONTENTS instead leaves the directory itself visible, which is what makes the negations
# below actually apply.
generated/*
# The shipped set (P08/P18): built, never committed; publish uploads it.
release/

# TWO EXCEPTIONS, and they are temporary. These predate their matchers being wired, so they
# CANNOT currently be regenerated — and between them they hold 2,265 bathymetry identifiers
# already resolved to lakes, 2,122 of them name-verified. Losing them would mean re-deriving
# work nobody has the tooling to re-derive yet.
#
# When pipeline/bathymetry/generate/match.py and pipeline/stocking/generate/match.py land,
# these become ordinary regenerable candidates and these two lines come out.
!generated/bathymetry/audit.json
!generated/stocking/identifier_audit.json
# T322 (owner 2026-10-30): the slough review's GENERATED inputs (finder candidates + width-rule pre-marks), moved
# here from handoff/; committed because the review app and the T322 apply step read them. The owner's own page verdicts
# are curation and live in ../curated/waters/slough_page_calls.json.
!generated/sloughs/
# T330 (owner 2026-10-30): the curation review's machine-written inputs (tidal candidates / pre-verify, DFO suggestions,
# entry split suggestions, the Q154 sample, the mined name candidates, the T185 proposals), moved here from handoff/;
# committed because the review app reads them. The app's own refused-saves log is runtime state, not committed.
!generated/review/
generated/review/refused-saves.jsonl
# T324 (owner 2026-11-05): the gauge REVIEW QUEUE (`pipeline.gauges.generate.promote` writes it beside the curated
# matches.json) is machine output, so it lives here, not in ../curated/. Committed because `check_curated --ci` reads it
# in CI (a queued station is not STALE). `generated/gauges/` is un-excluded only to reach this one file.
!generated/gauges/
generated/gauges/*
!generated/gauges/candidates.json

# The tree's own documentation — the map of what each subdirectory is and who writes it.
# It belongs beside the thing it describes, not only in pipeline/docs/.
!generated/README.md
# gov.bc.ca's own copies of the synopsis chapters, fetched for the print cross-check;
# the tests skip (naming the file) when they are absent. See quota_print.OFFICIAL_DIR.
source/official/

# BC outline cache (pipeline/atlas/splits/bc_boundary.py): derived from the gpkg, rebuilt on demand
source/bc_boundary.exact.*
# (T352) source maps per build (app/tools/sourcemaps.mjs): kept on this machine, never committed or served
sourcemaps/
